<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korea Investment launches $50 mln debt/equity fund.</title>
<headline>Korea Investment launches $50 mln debt/equity fund.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea Investment Trust Co said on Thursday it had established a $50 million fund to invest in South Korean bonds and shares.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that 60 percent of the fund would be invested in bonds and 30 percent in shares. The remaining amount will be invested in other financial instruments, including call loans.</p>
<p>The lead manager in the launching of the fund is Daishin Securities.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
